n_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:9b17895dbb3220d7932673a28670260639b95356e15ab6d97983c4541fe4fa94","file":"preprints/Classical-capacity-and-entropy-inequalities-for-generalized-amplitude-damping-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex","line":208,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"ba9b2f5562241faa8dc0b0a411eeab3ace0c53e1b2503117c391886365ff7ba1","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Classical-capacity-and-entropy-inequalities-for-generalized-amplitude-damping-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:9b17895dbb3220d7932673a28670260639b95356e15ab6d97983c4541fe4fa94","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Classical-capacity-and-entropy-inequalities-for-generalized-amplitude-damping-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex#L208"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor all $\\gamma,\\nu\\in[0,1]$ and every integer $n\\ge1$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:main}\n \\chi(\\A_{\\gamma,\\nu}^{\\otimes n})\n =n\\chi(\\A_{\\gamma,\\nu})\n =\\frac n{\\ln2}\\max_{0\\le p\\le1}\n \\{h((1-\\gamma)p+\\gamma\\nu)-g(v_{\\gamma,\\nu}(p))\\},\n\\end{equation}\nwhere\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:v-main}\n v_{\\gamma,\\nu}(p)\n =\\gamma\\nu(1-\\nu)+\\gamma(1-\\gamma)(p-\\nu)^2.\n\\end{equation}\nIn particular, $C(\\A_{\\gamma,\\nu})=\\chi(\\A_{\\gamma,\\nu})$.\nIf $p$ maximizes \\eqref{eq:main}, independent products of the two\nequiprobable signals\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:pair}\n \\phi_\\pm=\\sqrt{1-p}\\,\\ket0\\ \\pm\\sqrt p\\,\\ket1\n\\end{equation}\nattain the Holevo information at every block length."}
